Spec: LaserReady

Platform: TypeScript/React/Vite/Electron

Purpose:
  Free, open-source vector design editor for laser cutting workflows.
  Handles the design side — creating, editing, and arranging vector shapes —
  then exports industry-standard SVG files ready for laser control software.

Structure:
  ./src/features/shapes: Shape models, tools, and commands
  ./src/features/editor: Canvas controller, rendering, input, history, snapping
  ./src/features/ui: UI components, panels, toolbar, header
  ./src/features/io: SVG import and export
  ./src/features/persistence: Project files and auto-save
  ./src/store: Zustand store (shapes and UI slices)
  ./src/core: Math utilities, command interface, base tool class
  ./src/config: Constants, shortcuts, themes, laser modes
  ./src/i18n: Translation files (en, es, ca)
  ./src/hooks: Custom React hooks
  ./electron: Electron desktop wrapper

Must:
  All shape manipulation is undoable via the Command pattern.
  The application works entirely client-side with no backend.
  SVG export produces laser-software-compatible output with mm dimensions.
  UI is accessible (ARIA labels, keyboard navigation).
  State is persisted automatically via IndexedDB.
  The coordinate system uses pixels internally (96 DPI) and displays mm to users.
  All tools are activated via single-key shortcuts.
  Shapes support three laser modes: Cut (red), Score (blue), Engrave (black).

Must not:
  Implement machine control, GCode generation, or device communication.
  Implement image/raster processing or bitmap tracing.
  Introduce a backend server or network dependency for core features.
  Use native alert() or confirm() dialogs.
  Store secrets or sensitive data.
  Break existing tests when adding features.
